"""Render checked proof and provenance; no mathematical computation."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,fitz
from reportlab.platypus import SimpleDocTemplate,Paragraph,Spacer
from reportlab.lib.styles import ParagraphStyle
from reportlab.lib import colors
from reportlab.graphics.shapes import Drawing,Rect,String
from reportlab.pdfbase import pdfmetrics
from reportlab.pdfbase.ttfonts import TTFont
r=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;o=r/'reports';o.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
pdfmetrics.registerFont(TTFont('DV','/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf'))
pdfmetrics.registerFont(TTFont('DVB','/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf'))
pdfmetrics.registerFontFamily('DV',normal='DV',bold='DVB')
b=ParagraphStyle('body',fontName='DV',fontSize=8.6,leading=11.2,spaceAfter=8)
t=ParagraphStyle('title',fontName='DVB',fontSize=17,leading=22,spaceAfter=14)
def p(x):return Paragraph(x,b)
d=Drawing(500,120);svg=['<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="500" height="120" viewBox="0 0 500 120">']
rows=[(81,'Actual local symbols','Normalized finite and infinity places','Proper residues; constants and linear factors'),(42,'Factorization','Actual split numerator and denominator','Finite support; product including infinity is one'),(3,'F5 controls','Omit infinity: 2 / remove signs: 4','Corrected products: 1')]
for yy,title,a,c in rows:
 d.add(Rect(0,yy,500,34,fillColor=colors.HexColor('#eaf2f6'),strokeColor=colors.HexColor('#2c788e')))
 svg.append(f'<rect x="0" y="{120-yy-34}" width="500" height="34" fill="#eaf2f6" stroke="#2c788e"/>')
 for xx,y,txt,size in [(9,yy+17,title,7.2),(104,yy+21,a,6.9),(104,yy+7,c,6.8)]:
  d.add(String(xx,y,txt,fontName='DV',fontSize=size));svg.append(f'<text x="{xx}" y="{120-y}" font-size="{size}" font-family="DejaVu Sans,sans-serif">{html.escape(txt)}</text>')
svg.append('</svg>');(o/'p1-reciprocity.svg').write_text('\n'.join(svg)+'\n')
g=json.loads((r/'evidence/gate.json').read_text());a=json.loads((r/'evidence/attempts.json').read_text())
bf=json.loads((r/'evidence/binding-check.json').read_text())['observations'][0]
flow=[Paragraph('Rational-function tame reciprocity',t),
p('<b>Result.</b> Lean proves the product of actual normalized finite tame symbols and the infinity symbol is one for every pair of nonzero rational functions with split numerators and denominators. A finite product may use any set containing their roots. Actual finite support is proved before using finprod. Over every algebraically closed field, splitting is automatic and both the classical and corrected inverse products are one. No reciprocity conclusion is assumed. [pcc:unverified]'),
d,Spacer(1,9),
p('<b>Proper residues and actual generators.</b> At each a, the official normalized (X-a)-adic RatFunc valuation supplies the base ring. The auxiliary local model Y²+Y=(X-a)³ has a proved nonsingular point (a,0), derivative in Y equal to one, and a distinct negative point in every characteristic. Global nonsingularity of that auxiliary model is not claimed. The inherited proper residue fixes the coefficient field, is surjective and has the maximal ideal as kernel. It agrees with every realizing actual curve and point above a. Polynomial residues are actual evaluation at a. The normalized infinity residue and symbol agree with every realizing model. Constants and all linear factors have derived orders and proper symbol values. The ratio of any two monic linear factors has infinity residue one, giving the necessary symbol sign minus one. [pcc:unverified]'),
p('<b>Proof.</b> For a fixed finite root cover, the finite product times the infinity symbol is bimultiplicative and skew. Actual evaluation proves reciprocity on constant/constant, constant/linear and linear/linear generator pairs, including repeated roots. Official polynomial splitting gives the exact leading-coefficient times root-factor product. Actual numerator/denominator identities express every split rational unit in the subgroup generated by those factors. The two actual product characters then extend the generator result through subgroup closure. Numerator and denominator roots also give an explicit finite support bound over any field. This is the known factorization method, with no presumed residues or arbitrary square cancellation. [pcc:unverified]'),
p('<b>Controls.</b> Over F5, the constant 2 and X have finite symbol 2 and infinity symbol 3: the complete product is one, while omitting infinity leaves 2. For X and X-1, removing the local signs gives product 4, while the actual signed product is one. These use actual rational functions and proper symbol evaluation. Characteristic-two and characteristic-three linear-factor products also equal one, with infinity symbols 1 and 2 respectively. The controls refute incorrect deletions, without refuting a qualified source theorem. [pcc:unverified]'),
p('<b>Sources and remaining scope.</b> Fresh Gille–Szamuely PDF204–206/208–209 (printed190–192/194–195) text and all five individual page visuals: complete bounded proofs 7.2.1–4 and 7.2.8–10, including the displayed n=2 bilinearity argument. Earlier Milnor relations and every norm/base-change dependency were not all read; the field-norm identification proof of 7.2.5 was not displayed. Six KB calls and both Conductor attempts were unavailable (127), with bounded official and frozen-source fallback. Initial PDF extraction preceded the fresh KB fallback; that order is recorded. General closed-point residue norms, elliptic global reciprocity, arbitrary divisors, isogeny comparison, descent, canonical Tate and general MOV/Frey–Rück remain open. All fourteen targets remain active. [pcc:unverified]'),
p(f'<b>Checks.</b> Whole-project gate: {g["declarations"]} declarations, 11 modules (10 concrete, one official bridge), zero failures or trusted native evaluations. All316 predecessor pins match before/after19 states and the gate; eight failed states and the default-limit failures are retained. Final source warnings zero; 30 packages, no copies, hydration or lake update. Full{bf["full_characters"]}-character header SHA{bf["full_decl_sha256"]}; separate binding check: one complete, zero prefix, zero unresolved after completed gate. Lossless archive: {a["files"]} files, {a["unique_objects"]} objects, {a["compressed_bytes"]} bytes XZ, round-trip and actual restoration equal. Standard Lean foundations; no holes, custom axioms, native proof evaluation, raised limits, new global flags, waivers or frozen edits. Same host/prover and procedural binding provide no independent compiler/parser/physical-host assurance. Signed status unverified; zero paid compute. [pcc:unverified]')]
SimpleDocTemplate(str(o/'report.pdf'),pagesize=(595,842),leftMargin=44,rightMargin=44,topMargin=36,bottomMargin=36).build(flow)
doc=fitz.open(o/'report.pdf');pages=[]
for i,page in enumerate(doc):
 blocks=page.get_text('blocks');pages.append(dict(page=i+1,text_within_page=all(page.rect.contains(fitz.Rect(x[:4]))for x in blocks),text_characters=len(page.get_text())))
 page.get_pixmap(matrix=fitz.Matrix(1,1)).save('/workspace/scratch/p1-tame-reciprocity-report-page'+str(i+1)+'.png')
(o/'layout.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(pages=pages,visual_inspection='pending'),indent=2)+'\n')
print(json.dumps(dict(pages=len(pages),bytes=(o/'report.pdf').stat().st_size,layout=pages)))
